## Lore

The Warlords control who may build, sell and install bionics across most of
Russia, and so they control most of the country''s Cyber-Docs as well. A
Warlord Cyber-Doc is the surgeon who keeps a War Camp''s many partial and
full conversion cyborgs running, and who decides, on the Warlord''s behalf,
who gets augmented and with what.

They are much like Cyber-Docs anywhere, with one difference: constant
warfare has made them battlefield doctors. They diagnose in seconds, pull
out and replace or repair bionics on the spot, and move on to the next
casualty, often under fire. Others work in the Warlords'' cybernetics
factories, fitting new Cyborg Shocktroopers, or serve secretive units that
augment spies and special operatives.

The troops hold them in high regard, the cyborgs most of all, since a
Cyber-Doc may be the only thing between a wrecked ''Borg and the scrap heap.
They are also known as Cyber-Hacks, Machine-Docs and Field-Docs.

## GM Notes

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: a medical harness with many
pouches, two dozen throw-away paper surgical gowns, 12 three hour discs for
the recorder, a hand-held computerized blood pressure machine, six
unbreakable specimen containers, 100 pairs of disposable surgical gloves,
an energy rifle of choice, an energy pistol sidearm and a handful of
personal items. The four E-Clips on the sheet are two for each gun. The book
says several IRMSS without a number; the sheet lists one.

Cybernetics are the player''s choice. A new character may take one
mechanical-looking Multi-Optic eye and two sensory implants. Experienced
Cyber-Docs often have a bionic hand, or hand and arm, with a laser finger,
a retractable finger blade and a fingerjack; some add one or two extra
bionic arms with a partly rebuilt chest and spine.

Money is 2D6x1000 credits plus 3D6x100 credits of tradeable goods. Salary is
4000-6000 credits a month with the finest accommodations, food, drink and
services, plus special items as bonuses and bionics on request.

On assignment the Cyber-Doc may get a field hospital, a full hospital or a
bionics factory, every kind of cybernetic, implant, organ and bionic weapon,
and extra weapons, vehicles, medical assistants or protective troops.
Availability depends on the local commander, stock, location, casualties
and combat conditions; the Cyber-Doc is near the top of the priority list,
but supplies can still run short.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'warlord-cyber-doc');


